Hotel (within 20 km of BER)
- IntercityHotel Berlin Airport BER Terminal 1 & 2 (4★)
  - At Terminal 1–2, easiest possible arrival.
  - Dates: Nov 9–12 (3 nights).
  - Approx total: €286.45 for 3 nights (breakfast extra; current listing shows no free cancellation).
  - Check-in from 15:00, check-out by 12:00.
  - Fast S-Bahn into the city (S9 direct to Alexanderplatz/City East; ~30–35 min).
Would you like me to reserve this, or should I shortlist a few alternatives (e.g., different vibe/price, Köpenick riverside, or airport-adjacent options)?

What’s fun around the hotel (quick trips, all within ~30–45 min by S-Bahn/bus)
- TV Tower (Fernsehturm), Alexanderplatz: iconic views; tool shows it ~11.7 km from the hotel.
- East Side Gallery and Oberbaumbrücke: largest open-air mural section of the Berlin Wall; great riverside walk.
- Treptower Park and the Soviet War Memorial: grand monument and peaceful park along the Spree.
- Old Town Köpenick and Schloss Köpenick: cobbled streets, palace on an island, riverside cafés; very close to the airport area.
- Tempelhofer Feld: a decommissioned airport turned giant urban park—great for a unique Berlin vibe.
- Classic center sights: Museum Island, Unter den Linden, Brandenburg Gate, Reichstag dome, Gendarmenmarkt (all easy via S9 + short walks).

3-day sightseeing routes (easy, well-sequenced)

Day 1 (Sat, Nov 9) — arrival 13:00
- Drop bags (or check in after 15:00).
- East Side Gallery → walk to Oberbaumbrücke → S9 to Alexanderplatz.
- Sunset from TV Tower (around 16:25 in November; book timed tickets).
- Dinner in Nikolaiviertel or Hackescher Markt.

Day 2 — “Berlin Classics”
- Morning: Museum Island (Pergamon’s main halls are under renovation; Neues Museum, Altes Museum, Bode, Alte Nationalgalerie are open).
- Walk Unter den Linden → Brandenburg Gate → Reichstag dome (free but requires advance registration).
- Afternoon: Holocaust Memorial → Potsdamer Platz → Topography of Terror or Checkpoint Charlie.
- Evening: Gendarmenmarkt area for dinner/drinks.

Day 3 — pick a theme
- A) Köpenick + Müggelsee: old town, palace, riverside lunch; if weather is nice, continue to Müggelsee for lakeside walk.
- B) Wall & Alt Berlin: Berlin Wall Memorial (Bernauer Str.), then Prenzlauer Berg cafés/shops.
- C) Alternative Berlin: Kreuzberg lunch, walk the canal, Tempelhofer Feld for golden-hour stroll.

Getting around
- From BER T1-2, take S9 to city center (Alexanderplatz ~30–35 min).
- Consider a Berlin WelcomeCard ABC (72h) for unlimited public transport in zones ABC (includes the airport) and attraction discounts. It’s convenient for a 3-day stay.

Next steps
- Should I hold/book the IntercityHotel at the airport, or would you like 3–5 more hotel options within 20 km (tell me your budget range, star level, and whether you want free cancellation/breakfast)?
- Want me to lock in timed tickets (TV Tower, Reichstag dome) and map these daily routes to exact train lines/stops?

